To generate a table of contents automatically in a LaTeX document, you can use the `tableofcontents` command provided by the `tocloft` package. Here's an example of how to include it in your LaTeX document:

```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{tocloft}

\begin{document}

\tableofcontents
\newpage

\section{Introduction}
This section provides an overview of the document.

\section{Methodology}
Here, we describe the methods used in the study.

\section{Results}
The results section presents the findings of the research.

\section{Discussion}
In this section, we discuss the implications of the results.

\section{Conclusion}
We summarize the main findings and provide recommendations for future work.

\end{document}
```

In this example, the `\tableofcontents` command is placed right after the `\begin{document}` line, which generates the table of contents with the section titles and their corresponding page numbers. The `\newpage` command is used to ensure the table of contents starts on a new page.

