Here's a Java solution to determine if a given integer `n` is a power of three without using loops or recursion:

```java
public class PowerOfThree {

    public static boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
        if (n <= 0) {
            return false;
        }
        return (n & (n - 1)) == 0 && (long)n % 3 == 0;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println(isPowerOfThree(27)); // true
        System.out.println(isPowerOfThree(0));  // false
        System.out.println(isPowerOfThree(-1)); // false
    }
}
```

